<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.jvz_devx.encore-yt</id>
  <name>Encore</name>
  <summary>A native YouTube Music client</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.jvz-devx">
    <name>jvz-devx</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <description>
    <p>Encore is a YouTube Music app for the desktop, written in Rust. It has no browser engine: the interface is drawn on the GPU, the effects are shaders, and a built-in audio engine plays the music.</p>
    <p>Browse Home, Explore and your Library, search, build a queue, read timed lyrics and watch the Now Playing visualiser. It integrates with the desktop through media keys, the shell player widget, notifications and a tray icon.</p>
    <p>Encore is unofficial and not affiliated with YouTube or Google. It uses YouTube Music's private web API, so a change on YouTube's side can break it. It has no telemetry and no server of its own.</p>
  </description>
